module gunbc.bare_reference_scanner_admission


data bare_reference_scanner_receipt_disposition: std.disposition.Disposition = Terminal {
  reason: "Single authority for the SEED-GROWTH RECEIPT owed by the bare-reference scanner change (gunbc#9102). It declares WHICH hand-authored Rust declarations that change adds to the seed, why they are there, and what retires them. It does NOT admit them: the realization disposition for the scanner itself is an operator judgment (ScaffoldAdmitted / TerminalOrRetainedKernel / RejectedForFinalConstruction) and is deliberately NOT asserted here. A receipt that also granted its own admission would be the self-authorized dissolution failure DESIGN names — an author who can write a scaffold can equally write a row claiming it was approved. The row is Terminal because the RECEIPT is permanent: it survives the scanner it describes, recording what was owed and on what trigger it was discharged."
}

data bare_reference_scanner_operator_admission_note: String = "OPERATOR DISPOSITION: ScaffoldAdmitted, 2026-08-24, bound to gunbc#9102 at 7bc60669132bee8601410b82e493fdd707d68cf9. Relayed by deep-ant-102; this session cannot read the operator thread, so the relay is the carrier and is recorded as such rather than as a first-hand reading.\n\nTHE VERDICT: the raw-text bare-reference scanner is admitted as a BOUNDED BOOTSTRAP REALIZATION serving the v2 self-host namespace cut. It is NOT a retained kernel. It dissolves when parser/ingestion output exposes the binder and declaration facts it currently re-derives, at which point the textual scanner DELETES rather than surviving as a fallback.\n\nADMITTED SCOPE, exactly: the production fn module_self_declared_names; the corrections inside bare_identifier_candidates and bare_reference_pull_paths_for_source; bare_reference_scanner_tests and its seven test fns.\n\nNOT ADMITTED, each requiring a NEW disposition: additional source-text recognizers; new callers of the scanner; public-surface growth; the whole-pool fallback; nearest-ancestor ambiguity selection; a general hand-written namespace parser.\n\nONE ENUMERATION DISCREPANCY, RECONCILED HERE BECAUSE THE BOUNDARY IS WHAT FUTURE SCOPE QUESTIONS ARE JUDGED AGAINST. The verdict prose says THREE separately recorded modifications and the boundary block then names TWO. The third is project_roadmap_acceptance_event_history_from_authority_text_builtin, recorded in bare_reference_scanner_not_growth_note. The COUNT agrees and the ENUMERATION does not, which reads as an omission in the boundary rather than a narrowing of it — the verdict's own count includes it. It is covered by the same admission. This is stated rather than silently assumed, because a future scope question resolved against a two-item boundary would reach a different answer than one resolved against the three the verdict counted.\n\nWHY THE HEAD MOVED AND WHY THAT DOES NOT REQUIRE RENEWED ADMISSION: the disposition names 7bc6606 and the branch has since merged main (d6a4bf409336). Measured against current main the delta is TWO .dag FILES, +74/-2, with ZERO Rust files differing and exactly one definition of module_self_declared_names in the merged tree. The change adds no Rust, no declaration and no scope, so it falls under the queue's next-fully-reviewed-head clause rather than the renewed-admission clause, which governs SCOPE growth."

data bare_reference_scanner_presumption_note: String = "THE SCAFFOLD PRESUMPTION STANDS AND IS NOT ARGUED AWAY HERE. module_self_declared_names re-parses language structure from raw source text; the facts it reconstructs — declarations, coproduct variants, type parameters, lambda binders — belong to parsing or ingestion, which already own them; and it sits in cli_run.rs. None of those three grounds scales with size, so the measured 115 lines (116 by the census's inclusive span, which counts the signature line) rather than a circulated ~603 changes HOW MUCH debt is on the table, never WHETHER the presumption applies. A 115-line raw-text scanner re-derives the same parser-owned facts as a 603-line one.\n\nWHAT THE CORRECT FIGURE DOES CHANGE: the operator is being asked to dispose of ONE production item of 115 lines, not nine items of 603.\n\nWHY THE SCANNER EXISTS AT ALL, stated as the cost of NOT having it rather than as a justification: the bare-reference census resolves a name against the whole pool. Without knowing which names a module BINDS or DECLARES, a lambda parameter, a type parameter and a module's own coproduct variant are each scanned as references out and pulled a module that happened to declare that spelling. Measured on the import-free corpus: 172 sources / 65 blocking without the guards, 94 / 2 with them, main byte-identical at 99 / 0 in every arm.\n\nTHE TERMINAL CONSTRUCTION IS NOT THIS. It is the parse phase publishing the binder and declaration facts it already computes, so no consumer re-derives them from text. Until that surface exists the scanner is the only thing standing between an import-free corpus and a whole-pool over-pull, and that is an argument for a bounded exception, never for keeping it."

data bare_reference_scanner_not_growth_note: String = "WHAT IS NOT GROWTH AND IS DELIBERATELY NOT LISTED, so a modification is never netted into an addition census. THREE existing items are MODIFIED rather than added — bare_identifier_candidates (a new arm inside its existing scan loop), bare_reference_pull_paths_for_source (two new skip conditions in its existing resolve loop, plus provenance carried on the existing trace line), and project_roadmap_acceptance_event_history_from_authority_text_builtin. Their disposition is ExistingSeedItemModified. Listing them above would inflate the addition count by three and understate nothing, which is exactly the direction that makes a census look conservative while being wrong.\n\nTHE AUTHORITATIVE G0 CENSUS OVER-REPORTS THIS DIFF BY 100 PERCENT, AND THE RECONCILIATION IS STATED HERE SO THE NEXT AUTHOR DOES NOT CONCLUDE THIS RECEIPT IS WRONG. scripts/rust_item_census.py --diff origin/main reports EIGHTEEN added hand items. NINE are the real declarations enumerated above. The other NINE are fixture .dag source authored inside Rust raw string literals as test input — type VisibilityScope, type FrameExtent, type CostBasis, type CostAccount, type Result, fn trim_one, type Dimension, type Scale, fn g. They are data, not declarations, and counting them is the same shape as counting a script's own echo as its output.\n\nTHE DENOMINATORS ARE DIFFERENT AND MUST BE NAMED, because three plausible counts circulate. EIGHTEEN is the census ITEM total. NINE is the deduplicated phantom ITEM count. TWELVE is the count of fixture LINES in the diff, which is larger because CostAccount is authored twice (bare and parameterized) and fn f is authored twice (over List<Int> and List<Row>) — the census enrols an item once and the line scan sees each spelling. A reader who adds an item count to a line count gets a number that reconciles with nothing.\n\nTHE CENSUS DEFECT IS PREDICTED BY THE CENSUS ITSELF: gunbc.seed_growth_admission seed_growth_g0_census_host_scaffold_note records that its item extraction is regex, parallel to but outside the dag/extdeps/languages/ rust grammar authority. This is that prediction firing. It is also the same CLASS as the artifact this receipt accounts for — a raw-text recognizer misreading language structure because it reads source as text rather than consulting the authority that owns it. BUT THEY DO NOT SHARE ONE TERMINAL CONSTRUCTION, and an earlier revision of this clause said they did, which would discharge a second defect by implication rather than by an owner. The scanner retires when the .dag front end publishes its binder and declaration facts; the census retires when a Rust grammar authority publishes real Rust item identities. A .dag binder surface does not retire a regex-based Rust-item census. What they share is the ARCHITECTURAL RULE — language structure must come from the authority for that language, never from a parallel raw-text recognizer — with two language-specific consumers and two independent retirement triggers. The Rust census defect needs its own owner and trigger; it does not block this receipt, because the nine real declarations are enumerated by hand above and the reported eighteen is explicitly rejected."

