  ],
  reason: "WHY RUST IS STILL NEEDED HERE: the bare-reference census runs inside the seed's own source loader, deciding which files enter a closure BEFORE any parse result exists to consult. It cannot read a parse-phase binder surface that the closure it is constructing has not yet produced. That is a bootstrap ordering constraint, not seed-shrink debt.\n\nWHY IT IS ADMITTED AGAINST THE v1 FREEZE: gunbc.v1_maintenance_standing v1_seed_standing admits by PURPOSE — does the change serve the v2 self-host program. An import-free corpus is the namespace cut, and without these guards the cut's regen subject refuses with roughly 65 hard diagnostics. This is defect repair on the self-host path.\n\nHAND-ITEM DELTA: +9 FROM THE MERGE BASE bd84f6696, ENUMERATED ABOVE — ONE production item (module_self_declared_names) and EIGHT test scaffolding items (the module plus seven test fns). That is the AUTHORSHIP figure and it is what this receipt names, because those declarations are what was written and naming them is the receipt's whole purpose.\n\nAGAINST CURRENT MAIN THE FIGURE IS ZERO, AND THAT IS NOT A SECOND ACCOUNTING OF THE SAME DELTA — IT IS A DIFFERENT FACT ABOUT WHERE THE CODE ALREADY IS. All nine declarations are ALREADY ON MAIN. gunbc#9090 merged this PR's branch into its own (`Merge commit eb2ad48df706... into session/witty-lark-109`, carrying the five scanner commits by name) and SQUASH-merged to main at 2026-08-24T18:01:36Z as fd55f00bc6. Squash carries CONTENT, NOT ANCESTRY, so `git merge-base --is-ancestor` reports none of those commits on main while `git grep` finds the function and every test fn there byte-identical. Both answers are true of different questions, and reading the ancestry answer as an authorship answer is what first made the byte-identity look like an independent re-derivation by a second author. There is one author and one lineage.\n\nSO THIS RECEIPT IS NOT A PROPOSAL. IT IS THE ACCOUNTING FOR CODE THAT HAS ALREADY SHIPPED, and that inverts what a refusal does. Nothing in any .dag on main names module_self_declared_names, so the seed today carries a hand-written source scanner with no seed-growth receipt anywhere. Refusing this receipt does not remove the scanner from the seed — it deletes the accounting and leaves the code in place, which is the outcome that keeps the seed silently grown. Admitting it is what makes the seed honest about what already landed. The operator's disposition is therefore a decision about ACCOUNTING, not about admitting new code, and it should be made in those terms.\n\nWHAT THIS PR CONTAINS TODAY, measured eb2ad48..HEAD: two .dag files — this module and the roster row. The 413 lines of scanner are on main by the route above.\n\nNO OTHER .rs FILE CHANGES ON THIS BRANCH AT ALL, and the way that sentence was got wrong once is worth more than the sentence. Measured from the MERGE BASE (git diff bd84f66..HEAD), the branch touches exactly three files: this module, the roster row, and cli_run.rs. An earlier revision of this row named five generated mirrors as having moved on the branch. They had not. That reading came from diffing against origin/main, which puts main on the LEFT, so main's own commits since the branch point rendered as deletions authored here — the branch was behind main, not editing mirrors. The receipt then carried a false population, and a second session independently verified the generated-file exemption for five files this branch never touched: a correct verification of an invented premise, which is the failure mode where two parties agree and both are wrong. The rule this row now stands on: a branch delta is measured from the MERGE BASE, never from the moving tip, and a hand-LOC census that names a file must be reproducible by a command that states its base. A large share is the doc comments carrying the receipts for each guard and the census of the arm the shape rule cannot decide.\n\nWHAT THIS RECEIPT DOES NOT DO: it does not admit the scanner. The realization disposition is an operator judgment and fails closed in its absence — see bare_reference_scanner_receipt_disposition.",
  owning_dissolution_lane: "v1-hand-queue-drain" as gunbc.roadmap_model.RoadmapNodeId,
  trigger: "Delete all nine declarations when the parse phase publishes the binder and declaration facts this scanner re-derives from text — module-local declaration names, coproduct variant heads, declaration type parameters, and lambda binder names — so the source loader consults a parse-owned surface instead of scanning source. That is the same terminal construction bare_reference_scanner_presumption_note names, and it retires the scanner whole rather than shrinking it.",
  current_boundary: "gunbc.bare_reference_scanner_admission -> v1_compiler.cli_run module_self_declared_names -> v1_compiler.cli_run bare_reference_pull_paths_for_source -> the both-closure edge index"
}
